    "answer": {
      "short": "$112\\frac{1}{2}$ glassfuls: 112 full glasses and half another glass.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Total volume}&=18\\times1\\frac{1}{4}\\\\&=18\\times\\frac{5}{4}\\\\&=\\frac{45}{2}\\text{ L}\\\\\\text{Number of glassfuls}&=\\frac{45}{2}\\div\\frac{1}{5}\\\\&=\\frac{45}{2}\\times5\\\\&=\\frac{225}{2}\\\\&=112\\frac{1}{2}\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore, there are $112\\frac{1}{2}$ glassfuls: 112 full glasses and half another glass.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
